# Mini-GPT Scaling Lab

Mini-GPT Scaling Lab is a recruiter-facing ML engineering project that implements a GPT-2-style decoder-only Transformer from scratch in PyTorch, then wraps it in a small but serious experiment framework for tokenizer training, dataset preparation, training, evaluation, checkpointing, generation, tests, and a local Gradio demo.

The core Transformer is handwritten PyTorch: no `transformers.GPT2LMHeadModel`, no `AutoModelForCausalLM`, no `Trainer`, no `nn.TransformerEncoder`, and no `nn.MultiheadAttention`.

## What Is Implemented

- Causal self-attention with a lower-triangular mask
- Multi-head attention with manual Q/K/V projection and reshaping
- GPT-style Transformer blocks with LayerNorm, GELU MLPs, residual connections, dropout, and optional weight tying
- BPE tokenizer training with the Hugging Face `tokenizers` library
- Local text and TinyStories dataset preparation
- AdamW training loop with warmup, cosine decay, gradient accumulation, clipping, validation, perplexity, samples, and checkpointing
- Checkpoint resume and best/latest checkpoint saving
- Evaluation scripts and parameter counting
- Autoregressive generation with temperature, top-k, top-p, and repetition penalty
- Debug, tiny, small, and medium scaling configs
- Pytest coverage for attention masks, model shapes/loss, tokenizer round trips, checkpointing, sampling, generation, and tiny overfit behavior
- Lightweight Gradio demo

## Project Structure

```text
mini-gpt-scaling-lab/
├── configs/                 # Debug/tiny/small/medium YAML configs
├── data/                    # Tokenized datasets live here
├── checkpoints/             # Model checkpoints live here
├── notebooks/               # Original notebook plus architecture walkthrough
├── src/minigpt/             # Package source
├── scripts/                 # CLI entry points
├── app/                     # Gradio demo
├── reports/                 # Experiment notes, ablations, model card
├── tests/                   # Lightweight pytest suite
└── .github/workflows/       # CI
```

## Setup

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -U pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install -e .
```

## Common Commands

Train a tokenizer from local text:

```bash
python scripts/train_tokenizer.py \
  --config configs/debug.yaml \
  --input data/sample.txt \
  --output-dir artifacts/tokenizer \
  --vocab-size 256
```

Prepare a local text dataset:

```bash
python scripts/prepare_dataset.py --config configs/debug.yaml --input data/sample.txt
```

Prepare a small TinyStories sample:

```bash
python scripts/prepare_dataset.py --config configs/tiny.yaml
```

Train a debug model:

```bash
python scripts/train_model.py --config configs/debug.yaml
```

Train a tiny model:

```bash
python scripts/train_model.py --config configs/tiny.yaml
```

Resume training:

```bash
python scripts/train_model.py --config configs/tiny.yaml --resume checkpoints/tiny/latest.pt
```

Evaluate:

```bash
python scripts/run_eval.py --checkpoint checkpoints/tiny/best.pt --config configs/tiny.yaml
```

Sample:

```bash
python scripts/sample.py \
  --checkpoint checkpoints/tiny/best.pt \
  --prompt "Once upon a time" \
  --max-new-tokens 100 \
  --temperature 0.8 \
  --top-k 50
```

Run the demo:

```bash
python app/app.py
```

## Scaling Lab

| Config | Purpose | Approx Size | Context |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `debug.yaml` | Smoke tests and CPU sanity checks | <1M params | 64 |
| `tiny.yaml` | Local experiments with readable TinyStories outputs | 1M-3M params | 128 |
| `small.yaml` | More serious local/GPU runs | 8M-15M params | 256 |
| `medium.yaml` | Longer GPU-oriented run | 25M-50M params | 512 |

