## Ablation Plan

- Model size: debug vs tiny vs small vs medium
- Context length: 64, 128, 256, 512
- Tokenizer vocab size: small educational vocab vs larger BPE vocab
- Sampling strategy: greedy, top-k, top-p, temperature sweeps
- Learning rate schedule: warmup length, min LR, cosine decay

## Limitations

This is not full GPT-2 scale. Small models trained on TinyStories or tiny local corpora will not be ChatGPT-like. Output quality depends heavily on dataset size, training time, tokenizer quality, and available compute.

## Future Work

- Distributed training with DDP
- Larger corpora and cleaner data filtering
- Better evaluation harness beyond validation perplexity
- Quantized inference
- Hugging Face Hub model upload

## Resume Bullets

- Built a GPT-2-style decoder-only Transformer from scratch in PyTorch, including manual causal multi-head attention, residual Transformer blocks, tied embeddings, and autoregressive sampling.
- Developed an end-to-end LLM training framework with BPE tokenizer training, dataset preparation, AdamW optimization, cosine scheduling, checkpoint resume, evaluation, and Gradio inference demo.
- Added lightweight CI-grade tests covering causal masking, model shape/loss contracts, tokenizer round trips, checkpoint restoration, sampling, and tiny-batch overfitting.
